===Precedence of Banffozoa over Heteromorphida===

The question of whether the name Banffozoa or Heteromorphida takes precedence is muddied by two factors:
# The [[principle of priority]] for animal taxa does not formally apply to names above the rank of [[family (biology)|family]]<ref name="iczn1999">ICZN 1999 (International Code of Zoological Nomenclature, 1999 Ed.).</ref>
# The relevant publication date for Banffozoa is unclear

Banffozoa {{small|Caron 2006}} was published in a journal issue dated June 2005:

: Earth and Environmental Science Transactions of The Royal Society of Edinburgh , Volume 96 , Issue 2 , June 2005 , pp. 95 - 111<ref>{{cite web|website=Cambridge Core |title=''Banffia constricta'', a putative vetulicolid from the Middle Cambrian Burgess Shale {{!}} Cambridge Core |date=July 26, 2007 |accessdate=December 10, 2024 |url=https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/earth-and-environmental-science-transactions-of-royal-society-of-edinburgh/article/abs/banffia-constricta-a-putative-vetulicolid-from-the-middle-cambrian-burgess-shale/BE8BE09A5025A6535DBFB1E2A78E4E82}}</ref>

However the article itself carries in-print citation with a formal year of 2006:

: ''Transactions of the Royal Society of Edinburgh: Earth Sciences,'' '''96''', 95–111, 2006 (for 2005)<ref>{{harvnb|Caron|2005|page=95|loc=header text}}</ref>

Online citation databases appear to prefer the 2005 date.<ref>{{cite web|website=Semantic Scholar |title=Banffia constricta, a putative vetulicolid from the Middle Cambrian Burgess Shale {{!}} Semantic Scholar |accessdate=December 10, 2024 |url=https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/Banffia-constricta%2C-a-putative-vetulicolid-from-the-Caron/e6fac19f8fb8be0006bad4486d08e7d48bafc1de}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|website=Google Scholar |title=Banffia constricta, a putative vetulicolid from the... - Google Scholar |accessdate=December 10, 2024 |url=https://scholar.google.com/scholar?hl{{=}}en&as_sdt{{=}}0%2C5&q{{=}}Banffia+constricta%2C+a+putative+vetulicolid+from+the+Middle+Cambrian+Burgess+Shale&btnG{{=}}}}</ref>

Heteromorphida {{small|Shu 2005}} was published with a date of October 2005.  <ref>{{cite web|website=Springer Nature Link |accessdate=December 10, 2024 |title=On the Phylum Vetulicolia {{!}} Science Bulletin |url=https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/BF03183746}}</ref>

This appears to have led to some confusion, with Aldridge ''et al.'' (2007) emending Banffozoa to encompass both ''Banffia'' and ''Heteromorphus'', but then adding a note in proof that Heteromorphida appears to have precedence based on comparing the October date to the formal 2006 date of Caron's article.<ref>{{harvnb|Aldridge|Hou|Siveter|Siveter|2007|page=168}}</ref>  However, the October 2005 date is later than the actual June 2005 date of the issue that published the name Banffozoa.



